    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess, but that sounds like something people just tell themselves to stay distracted. when you look at the math, it's hard to see the \"passion\" as anything more than a temporary fluctuation. like, why bother maintaining the structure of a life if the cosmic scale is just going to flatten it all out anyway? it feels like we're just burning fuel for no reason. doesn't it seem more logical to just stop fighting the inevitable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
